+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Static ("no-render") chart-specification linter
+#
+# The rules below inspect a chart tree without ever calling ``to_dict()``,
+# hitting the Vega-Lite compiler, or looking at the data.  Their valid-value
+# sets come from the Vega-Lite JSON schema that ships with this package
+# (``altair/vegalite/v6/schema/vega-lite-schema.json``): the frozen sets
+# here are kept in-file so linting is cheap and deterministic and does not
+# depend on the (large) schema document being parsed at runtime.
+#
+# Historically these checks either fired far too late (schema validation,
+# the Vega-Lite compiler in the browser) or not at all (silent no-ops when
+# a channel name is unknown, when a scale is incompatible with the field
+# type, ...).  The linter exposes them at ``altair.lint`` / ``chart.lint``
+# and, when the caller asks for it, wires them into ``to_dict`` /
+# ``to_json`` via the ``strict_lint`` keyword argument.
